,"forks":1,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"In the fields of computational linguistics and probability, an n-gram is a contiguous sequence of n items from a given sequence of text or speech. The items can be phonemes, syllables, letters, words or base pairs according to the application. The n-grams typically are collected from a text or speech corpus. When the items are words, n-grams may also be called shingles.[1]  An n-gram of size 1 is referred to as a \"unigram\"; size 2 is a \"bigram\" (or, less commonly, a \"digram\"); size 3 is a \"trigram\". Larger sizes are sometimes referred to by the value of n, e.g., \"four-gram\", \"five-gram\", and so on.","topics":[],"score":229768,"global_rank":113350},{"name":"anirudhajith/2048","owner":"anirudhajith","html_url":"https://github.com/anirudhajith/2048","stars":0,"forks":1,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"This is a Python implementation of the popular sliding block puzzle game called 2048.","topics":[],"score":229768,"global_rank":113353},{"name":"mikepschneider/circuitpy_ms","owner":"mikepschneider","html_url":"https://github.com/mikepschneider/circuitpy_ms","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"CircuitExpress Demo And Timer Code","topics":[],"score":229767,"global_rank":113357},{"name":"SiriRaavi/steering_angle_prediction","owner":"SiriRaavi","html_url":"https://github.com/SiriRaavi/steering_angle_prediction","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":["prediction","self-driving-car","steering-angle"],"score":229767,"global_rank":113362},{"name":"prismofeverything/organism-legacy","owner":"prismofeverything","html_url":"https://github.com/prismofeverything/organism-legacy","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":2,"issues":8,"language":"Python","description":"implementation of the organism board game","topics":[],"score":229744,"global_rank":113380},{"name":"kassiwinter/project-agent-s